course: dictionary
lesson: 9921
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tang has more than one meaning. Context, the words around it, tells you which one is meant. «The lemon gave the drink a bright tang.» Here a tang is a strong, sharp taste, like lemon.
explain: «There was a tang of autumn in the air.» Here tang means a small hint or trace of something. You can notice it, but it is not very strong. Ask yourself: what does the sentence feel like, and which meaning fits best?
explain: A capital letter can change everything. «The Tang dynasty ruled China long ago.» Tang is a name here. A dynasty is a family whose rule passes from parent to child, so this Tang is a royal family, not a taste. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
fact: A tang is a strong, sharp taste or smell, like lemon or the sea air.
fact: «Tangy» is the adjective: «tangy cheese» has a sharp, fresh taste.
fact: «A tang of autumn» means a small hint of autumn.
fact: The Tang dynasty was a great Chinese family of rulers, famous for poetry, art and trade.
fact: The tang of a knife is the part of the blade that fits into the handle.
exercise: «The salty tang of the sea filled the air.» What does tang mean here? | A cold wind | *A strong, sharp taste or smell | A sandy beach | A loud noise
exercise: «The tangy cheese made my mouth water.» What kind of taste is tangy? | Sweet and sticky | Bland and dry | Warm and soft | *Sharp and fresh
exercise: «There was a tang of autumn in the air.» What does tang mean in this sentence? | A royal family in China | A big, loud storm | A sharp knife blade | *A small hint or trace of something
test: «The Tang dynasty was famous for poetry, art and trade.» What is the Tang dynasty? | A strong smell of lemons | *A great Chinese family of rulers | A sweet cake from the market | A fish that lives on coral reefs
test: Which sentence uses tang to mean a sharp taste? | «The Tang dynasty ruled China long ago.» | *«The lemon gave the drink a bright tang.» | «The tang of the knife fits inside the handle.» | «The tang of the sea was mild and quiet.»
exam: What does tang mean in «The knife's tang fits inside its handle»? | A royal family in China | A small hint of something | *The part of the blade that fits into the handle | A strong, sharp taste
